<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Crush pick-up weighs on basis.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Crush pick-up weighs on basis.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A sharp pick-up in the reported weekly crush put soybean meal basis levels on the defensive with some locations already weakening and others possibly poised to decline early next week, dealers said.</p>
<p>The National Oilseed Processors Association put the crush for the week to May 28 at 25.46 million bushels, up from 22.79 million a week earlier and significantly above expectations.</p>
<p>Dealers said the increase was due partly to improved margins, while several key plants had also resumed production after downtime. Margins have since dwindled slightly and a modest decline in crush is anticipated for the week to June 4.  </p>
